exempt       = (input('exempt_assets') || {})['CKV_AWS_175'] || []

control 'CKV_AWS_175' do
  title 'Ensure WAF has associated rules'

  desc <<~DESC
    Checkov asserts this against Terraform. This profile asserts it against
    the aws_waf_web_acl resources that actually exist, read through the
    stock inspec-aws aws_waf_web_acl resource.
  DESC

  desc 'rationale', <<~RATIONALE
    A web ACL with no rules inspects nothing. It is attached, it appears in
    the architecture diagram and it shows up as a control in the SSP, and
    every request reaching the protected resource passes through it
    untouched.
  RATIONALE

  desc 'check', <<~CHECK
    Checkov looks for: Ensure WAF has associated rules
  CHECK

  desc 'fix', <<~'FIX'
    Terraform — aws_waf_web_acl:

      resource "aws_waf_web_acl" "app" {
        name        = "app"
        metric_name = "app"

        default_action {
          type = "ALLOW"
        }

        rules {
          priority = 1
          rule_id  = aws_waf_rule.sql_injection.id
          type     = "REGULAR"

          action {
            type = "BLOCK"
          }
        }
      }

    Out of band — aws_waf_web_acl:

      aws waf update-web-acl --web-acl-id <id> --change-token "$(aws waf get-change-token --query ChangeToken --output text)" --updates 'Action=INSERT,ActivatedRule={Priority=1,RuleId=<rule-id>,Action={Type=BLOCK},Type=REGULAR}'

    Note (aws_waf_web_acl): This is the WAF Classic form, because WAF Classic is
    the only WAF type this control can enumerate — wafv2's list call requires a
    Scope argument the enumerator cannot supply. WAF Classic is deprecated: a
    new ACL should be an aws_wafv2_web_acl with at least one rule block (an AWS
    managed rule group is the usual starting point), and this control will NOT
    assess it.
  FIX

  tag checkov_id:            'CKV_AWS_175'
  tag checkov_category:      'APPLICATION_SECURITY'
  tag checkov_version:       '3.3.16'
  tag checkov_kind:          'custom'
  tag tf_resources:          %w[aws_waf_web_acl aws_wafregional_web_acl aws_wafv2_web_acl]
